Your intuition is right about the computer analogy up to a point. If you buy a machine with a better processor, more RAM, faster storage, etc., you can make its capacity higher. But putting more specifications on the machine doesn't automatically make the machine a world-class engineer.

AI is similar.

You can give a model enormous capability and enormous instructions, but capability ≠ reliable expertise.

